<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congress of Vienna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1815">1815</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Congress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> was a conference of European powers held in 1814–1815 to reorganise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I</a> played a dominant role, establishing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> as one of the five great powers. The congress also partially restored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>, while confirming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s retention of the Cape and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna.jpg" alt="Congress of Vienna" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander Altenhof · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Europe_1815_map_en.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
